# What the Reader should expose for word-basic.pdf, written from what the
# document means — never generated from the Reader's output. Rendered with the
# interface in Japanese, which is where `document lang=ja`, the region's name,
# the page separator's wording and the link's new-tab note come from.
#
# Conventions this follows, from how renderer.tsx presents a document:
#   - The document title is the page's h1, outside the article, and appears
#     once. The Title-style paragraph at the top of the body is the same text
#     and must not be read a second time — whether the tags call it a heading
#     (which `dropLeadingTitleHeading` removes) or a paragraph (which it does
#     not).
#   - Content headings sit one level below the title: Word's Heading 1 is h2.
#   - A list item's text is a paragraph inside the item.
#   - The table's first column is row headers: the .docx turns on the
#     "First Column" table style option, and Word tags those cells TH.
#   - Every table sits in a region named 表, so it can scroll by keyboard.
#   - The separator before page 2 is a paragraph, in the tree by design.
#   - A link's name carries the Reader's note that it opens a new tab, and so
#     does the sentence it is part of.
#
# Absent by intent: the running header (ヘッダー：検証用文書), the footer
# (フッター N), and the decorative divider — no img and no empty figure.
document lang=ja title="アクセシビリティ検証用文書 その1（リーダー） — Accessible PDF View"
  banner
    heading level=1 "アクセシビリティ検証用文書 その1"
  main
    region "リーダー"
      article lang=ja
        heading level=2 "はじめに"
        paragraph "この文書は、Accessible PDF View の動作を確かめるために作成したものです。"
        paragraph "詳しくは、Accessible PDF View のサイト（新しいタブで開きます）をご覧ください。"
          link href=https://accessiblepdfview.org/ "Accessible PDF View のサイト（新しいタブで開きます）"
        heading level=2 "確認する要素"
        heading level=3 "箇条書き"
        paragraph "次の項目を確認します。"
        list
          listitem
            paragraph "見出しの階層"
          listitem
            paragraph "箇条書きと番号付きリスト"
            # Known gap (producer): Word does not tag this nesting. See
            # known-gaps.ts.
            list
              listitem
                paragraph "入れ子の箇条書き"
          listitem
            paragraph "見出しセルのある表"
        heading level=3 "番号付きリスト"
        # One list of three, even if Word tags each numbered paragraph as a
        # list of its own.
        list ordered
          listitem
            paragraph "PDF を開く"
          listitem
            paragraph "構造を読み取る"
          listitem
            paragraph "HTML として表示する"
        heading level=3 "表"
        paragraph "表1は、文書の要素と PDF のタグ、HTML の要素の対応です。"
        region "表"
          table
            row
              columnheader "要素"
              columnheader "PDF のタグ"
              columnheader "HTML の要素"
            row
              rowheader "見出し"
              cell "H1〜H6"
              cell "h1〜h6"
            row
              rowheader "箇条書き"
              cell "L、LI"
              cell "ul、li"
            row
              rowheader "表"
              cell "Table、TR、TH、TD"
              cell "table、tr、th、td"
        heading level=3 "図"
        paragraph "図1は、月ごとの閲覧数を示した棒グラフです。"
        # Letter-size page 1 has no room left for the chart.
        paragraph "2 ページ"
        figure
          img "月ごとの閲覧数の棒グラフ。4月120、5月180、6月150、7月240で、7月が最も多い。"
        heading level=4 "装飾の画像"
        paragraph "すぐ上の横線は装飾として指定した画像なので、文書の構造には含まれないはずです。"
        # The manual page break: the heading says 2ページ目 but it lands on page 3.
        paragraph "3 ページ"
        heading level=2 "2ページ目"
        paragraph "本文は2ページ目に続きます。ヘッダーとフッターの文字は、本文には含まれないはずです。"
